# The baselines tools/compatdiff compares this tree with (#100).
#
# Read by `make compat-diff` and `make compat-md`, and by the required `compat
# guard` CI job on every pull request into this line. Read strictly: a line that
# is not one of the two below, separated by single spaces, is an error.
#
#   main <sha>             Check A, parity: main's commit this line's exported
#                          API is compared with. Forty hex digits, and it must
#                          be on main -- a pin into this line's own history would
#                          compare the line with itself.
#   release <tag> <sha>    Check B, compatibility: a published release of this
#                          line. Every feature it exported must still be here,
#                          unchanged. The tag must name exactly that commit.
#                          One line per release, and a line is never removed:
#                          a published release has callers forever.
#
# WHY PINS, and not main's tip or the newest tag: a check that read either would
# let an unchanged commit here turn red because of a merge somewhere else. Both
# move by a reviewable change to this file. Advancing main's pin is a port: every
# difference the new commit brings is either ported or listed in carveouts.txt,
# in the same pull request -- and testdata/behavior_vectors.json is taken from
# main at the new pin, since `make compat-diff` holds it there byte for byte as committed
# (#104, vectors.go), and this line's binding has to pass it. A release's line is added once its tag exists, in
# the pull request after the release (docs/release.md), and `make compat-diff`
# fails on any v1.x tag in the clone that this file does not name -- except, in
# the CI run that pushing a tag starts, that tag, which names the release itself.
#
# main's pin was 5e40964, the commit the whole parity epic (#88) ports from and
# the one tools/contractdrift/main.pin still names, until #104 advanced it to
# 676486c, main's merge of the behaviour vectors. Between the two, main changed
# CI and docs (#124, which this line had already taken as #122) and added the
# vectors, and changed no exported declaration. The two pins are separate on
# purpose: each advances with the work that has to come with it, which for one
# is the contract gate's files and for the other is this line's API and its
# vectors.

main 676486caf50bbdc0dd9655f09e228e086411f6ca
release v1.0.0 ad3ced172994940edaccfa3e52e2d76060e4e9c4
release v1.1.0 483ad84659b70ee281aef593a17e7792bdd24d68
